// Only justified branches with supported methods may run. Future integration.
title Where physics fits - future calculations
direction down
colorMode pastel
styleMode plain
typeface clean
textSize medium

Cargo [label: "CHEMICAL + CONDITIONS\nLPG / CNG / propylene\nTransport or storage", color: blue]
Source [label: "SOURCE TERM\nWhat escapes?\nHow fast and for how long?", color: blue]
Select [shape: diamond, label: "SELECT A JUSTIFIED EVENT\nOnly supported methods\nNot every branch applies", color: orange]
Gas [label: "GAS DISPERSION\nWhere gas spreads\nValley physics: later work", color: purple]
Fire [label: "FIRE RADIATION\nHeat reaching\nnearby locations", color: purple]
Blast [label: "EXPLOSION OVERPRESSURE\nPressure above ambient\nEligible explosion only", color: purple]
Burst [label: "VESSEL FAILURE\nRupture + fragments\nSeparate model needed", color: purple]
Output [label: "EXPLAIN RESULTS\nUnits + time + limitations\nMap and authority review", color: green]

Cargo > Source
Source > Select
Select > Gas: Unignited release
Select > Fire: Applicable fire
Select > Blast: Applicable explosion
Select > Burst: Applicable rupture
Gas > Output
Fire > Output
Blast > Output
Burst > Output

// Missing inputs or unsupported conditions block a prediction; explain why.
// Gas buoyancy depends on release conditions, not only chemical identity.
// A 3D map is not a valley-flow model. Independent research is not field validated.
